      "side": 1,
      "message": "since the SkVertices object is only storing SkColor already, and not SkColor4f\u0027s, we can save bandwidth by having the VertexAttribType be kUByte4_norm and the SkSLType can be kHalf4.\n\nUnfortunately, we can\u0027t just write SkColor to VertexWriters and have them work out correctly due to machine endian-ness. We only support little endian, so that means an SkColor gets split into B,G,R,A whereas the GPU wants to interpret them as rgba. We can either call the helper function SkSwizzle_RB as we write them to the buffer, or we can use a swizzle in SkSL, so your assignment to the varying would be `color \u003d vertColor.bgra` to swap the B and R channels. This looks like the approach that\u0027s used in Ganesh, which minimizes CPU work.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 83
      },
