      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T01:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SkSL and the effect pipeline generally operate on premul colors, so they\u0027ve had alpha multiplied. SkColor and SkColor4f are not premul. Sometimes we can fold the premultiply into the color space transform, but since DrawVertices may skip that and the primitive color we\u0027re writing to is general purpose, I think it makes sense to make sure it\u0027s premul here.\n\nThis also makes it consistent with how the Ganesh drawmeshop handles it, where its color varying is premul. This means that the colors are interpolated in premul, which can work out to different gradient than if they were unpremul (generally nicer to interpolate pre-multiplied).\n\nIf we were to combine this with the SkSL swizzling mentioned above, this would look like `color \u003d half4(vertColor.bgr * vertColor.a, vertColor.a);` or I believe we can simply do `color \u003d premul(vertColor.bgra);`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "d4f1d12c8ad4be8534ec06816470b0a14f0ed3cf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
